ZBar
----
zbar.wasm is a WebAssembly build of ZBar bar code reader, version 0.23.90.
Repository: https://github.com/mchehab/zbar
License:    LGPL-2.1-or-later
License text: LICENSE.LGPL-2.1.txt in this directory (GNU Lesser General
            Public License, version 2.1, full text)
            (also https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.txt and
            https://github.com/mchehab/zbar/blob/master/LICENSE.md)

Because ZBar is licensed under the LGPL, you may replace it with your own
build of ZBar (see "How to reproduce" below) and the scanner will keep
working. zbar.wasm and zbar.js must be replaced TOGETHER: zbar.js is the
Emscripten glue generated for that exact zbar.wasm build and does not work
with a binary from another build.

koder.js
--------
koder's JavaScript wrapper (public/wasm/koder.js, MIT) is NOT shipped here.
The wrapper logic (CreateKoder + cwrap of createBuffer, deleteBuffer,
triggerDecode, getScanResults, getResultType) is derived from koder.js at the
commit above and rewritten in ES5 into src/cam-scanner.js (ZbarKoder), so the
library keeps its browser floor; the original uses a top-level class and the
ES2021 ||= operator. zbar.js and zbar.wasm remain unmodified.

